<title>FRANCE: AGF unit acquires Austrian insurer.</title>
<headline>AGF unit acquires Austrian insurer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coface, 58 percent held by Assurances Generales de France (AGF), said on Tuesday that it had raised its stake in Austrian insurer Oesterreichische Kreditversicherung (OKV) to 79.2 percent from 30 percent.</p>
<p>OKV is the biggest credit insurer in the Austrian market with a 50 percent share, representing around 226 million French francs of turnover, Coface said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not disclose the terms of the transaction.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
